This project (ZeroMem / legacy package alias v2-memory) is designed as a
zero-dependency local memory engine paired with Qwen3.5-4B-Memory-V2
(https://huggingface.co/IMLIULIAN/qwen3.5-4b-memory-v2), which is a derivative
work based on Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B (Apache-2.0).

Schema Lineage & Third-Party Ecosystem Compatibility:
The structured fact-extraction and pre-write admission schema conventions used
in ZeroMem (including bank/namespace partitioning, fact types
"world" / "experience" / "observation", temporal fields occurred_start /
occurred_end / mentioned_at, and where / entities metadata) are inspired by and
conceptually compatible with Vectorize Hindsight
(https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight, MIT License). ZeroMem's single-file
SQLite/FTS5 storage engine, deterministic guardrails, admission loop, timeline
supersession store, credential redaction, export/backup utilities, MCP server,
and desktop workbench are independent clean-room implementations containing no
Hindsight source code.

Name Disambiguation:
ZeroMem (零忆, by B站IM榴莲 / IMLIULIAN / ZeroZoneX) is an independent open-source
local memory engine and is not affiliated with, derived from, or related to the
academic paper "Zero-Mem: Zero-Token Memory Operations for LLM Agents"
(Yilin Xiao et al., arXiv:2607.29377, July 2026).
